    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Murphy returns for his twelve-week review. He finished Cognitive Processing Therapy with Dr. Lee last week after nine sessions and still uses the worksheets when an old belief about blame or danger comes up. His nightmares now come about once a week. He falls asleep within about 20 minutes on most nights, wakes once on some nights and gets back to sleep quickly, and sleeps about six and a half to seven hours. He now goes to crowded places he used to avoid and is concentrating well at work. His mood is good. He has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm since his last visit, still carries his safety plan, and the lethal-means steps remain in place. He uses no alcohol, drugs, medicines, or sleep aids. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Therapy course completed; fewer nightmares; less avoidance</td></tr><tr><td>Nightmares</td><td>About once a week</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Asleep in about 20 minutes; six and a half to seven hours; wakes once on some nights</td></tr><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Nine Cognitive Processing Therapy sessions completed last week</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, or plan since the last visit; safety plan kept</td></tr><tr><td>Substances</td><td>No alcohol, drugs, medicines, or sleep aids</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

